From: Vadim Deiss <letechnarb@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath11k: nss: learn the addresses behind a WDS station

A device bridged behind a 4addr (WDS) station gets no traffic: frames to
its address need an AST entry pointing at the station, and ath11k adds
one only when the NSS firmware reports the address as WDS_LEARN.

NSS firmware 12.5-210 on IPQ5018 never sends WDS_LEARN for a station on
an AP_VLAN ext vdev. It counts the frame as a WDS source port exception
and hands it up on the ext vdev as plain data, so frames to the device
are never sent.

Remember the WDS peer of the ext vdev when set_4addr_wk() brings it up.
For an Ethernet frame on the ext vdev whose source address is neither
the station's own nor in its AST list, run the learning of
ath11k_nss_wds_type_rx(), split out to run under the base_lock of the
peer lookup. The split-out code now sends the NSS update for a move only
if ath11k_peer_update_ast() succeeded. ECM-accelerated flows do not come
up on the ext vdev, so the lookup only runs on the host path.

Tested on a Xiaomi AX6000 (NSS FW 12.5-210) with a QCA9887 as the 4addr
client and a bridged MAC behind it, on QCN9074 and on the IPQ5018 radio:
the device behind the client went from no replies to ping in both
directions over IPv4 and IPv6, and its TCP flow to a wired host is
accelerated by ECM.

Link: https://github.com/kuncy7/openwrt-nss-edma/issues/87

Signed-off-by: Vadim Deiss <letechnarb@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/nss.h
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/nss.h
@@ -232,6 +232,8 @@ struct arvif_nss {
 	bool added;
 	/* Flag to notify if ext vdev is up/down */
 	bool ext_vdev_up;
+	/* Peer id of the WDS station bound to this ext vdev, -1 if none */
+	int wds_peer_id;
 #ifdef CPTCFG_ATH11K_NSS_SUPPORT
 	/* Keep the copy of di_type for nss */
 	enum nss_dynamic_interface_type di_type;
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/nss.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/nss.c
@@ -753,13 +753,66 @@ static bool vdev_check_local_dev(u8 *wds
 	return false;
 }
 
+/* Add or move the AST entry of a source address seen behind ta_peer.
+ * Called with base_lock held.
+ */
+static void ath11k_nss_wds_learn_sa(struct ath11k *ar, struct net_device *dev,
+				    struct ieee80211_vif *vif,
+				    struct ath11k_peer *ta_peer, u8 *src_mac,
+				    u8 is_sa_valid)
+{
+	struct ath11k_ast_entry *ast_entry;
+
+	lockdep_assert_held(&ar->ab->base_lock);
+
+	ast_entry = ath11k_peer_ast_find_by_addr(ar, src_mac);
+
+	/*
+	 * If WDS update is coming back on same peer it indicates that it is not roamed
+	 * This situation can happen if a MEC packet reached in Rx direction even before the
+	 * ast entry installation in happend in HW
+	 */
+	if (ast_entry) {
+		if (ast_entry->peer && (ast_entry->peer->peer_id == ta_peer->peer_id) && (vif->type == NL80211_IFTYPE_STATION))
+			return;
+	}
+
+	/*
+	 * Avoid WDS learning if src mac address matches
+	 * any of local netdevice mac address.
+	 */
+	if (vif->type == NL80211_IFTYPE_AP || vif->type == NL80211_IFTYPE_AP_VLAN) {
+		if (vdev_check_local_dev(src_mac))
+			return;
+	}
+
+	if (!is_sa_valid) {
+		ath11k_peer_add_ast(ar, ta_peer, src_mac,
+				    ATH11K_AST_TYPE_WDS);
+		if (!ta_peer->nss.ext_vdev_up)
+			ieee80211_rx_nss_notify_4addr(dev, ta_peer->addr);
+	} else {
+		if (!ast_entry) {
+			ath11k_peer_add_ast(ar, ta_peer, src_mac,
+					    ATH11K_AST_TYPE_WDS);
+			if (!ta_peer->nss.ext_vdev_up)
+				ieee80211_rx_nss_notify_4addr(dev, ta_peer->addr);
+		} else if (ast_entry->type == ATH11K_AST_TYPE_WDS) {
+			/* Tell NSS only about a move the host made: the entry
+			 * may not be mapped yet, or its peer may be going.
+			 */
+			if (!ath11k_peer_update_ast(ar, ta_peer, ast_entry))
+				ath11k_nss_update_wds_peer(ar, ta_peer, src_mac);
+		}
+	}
+}
+
